 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "The perfect locus with fixed degree",
 "statement": "Let $X$ be a scheme and let $E\\in D(\\mathcal{O}_X)$ be\nperfect. Given $i,r\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ there is\nan open subscheme $U\\subseteq X$ characterized by the property: a\nmorphism $f:Y\\to X$ factors through $U$ if and only if $Lf^*E$ is\nisomorphic to a locally free $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-module of rank $r$ placed in\ndegree $i$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-picard-framework/sk-thm-picard-perfect/lem-pc-perfect-locus.md",
  "place": "node lem-pc-perfect-locus, order 681"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-pc-base-change",
  "def-pc-derived-category",
  "def-pc-derived-pullback",
  "def-pc-invertible-in-degree-zero",
  "def-pc-morphism-conventions"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "If $r<0$, take $U=\\varnothing$. Otherwise let $x\\in X$. By\n[def-pc-perfect-complex], near $x$ the object $E$ is represented\nby a bounded complex $M^\\bullet$ of finite free modules: the finitely\nmany projective terms can all be made free after shrinking.\nOver the local ring $\\mathcal O_{X,x}$, if a matrix of a differential\nhas a unit entry, row and column operations put that entry in a\n$1\\times1$ identity block. The equations $d^{j+1}d^j=0$ and\n$d^jd^{j-1}=0$ force the adjacent maps into and out of this block\nto be zero. Hence a contractible two-term summand splits off.\nEach operation decreases the sum of the ranks of the terms by two,\nso after finitely many operations the remaining complex has every\ndifferential matrix in the maximal ideal.",
   "uses": [
    "def-pc-perfect-complex"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Its residue-field differential is zero. Therefore, if\n$H^j(E\\otimes^{\\mathbf L}\\kappa(x))$ vanishes for $j\\ne i$ and\nhas dimension $r$ in degree $i$, the remaining free terms have\nrank zero except in degree $i$, where the rank is $r$.\nAll the changes of bases and the inverses of unit entries used in\nthis finite calculation are defined on an open neighbourhood of\n$x$. On that neighbourhood $E$ is consequently quasi-isomorphic\nto $\\mathcal O^{\\oplus r}[-i]$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "Define $U$ to be the set of points satisfying this residue-field\ncohomology condition. The preceding construction proves that $U$\nis open and that $E|_U$ is locally a free rank-$r$ module in degree\n$i$. Such local descriptions agree on overlaps through the\ncohomology sheaf $H^i(E)|_U$, which is therefore locally free of\nrank $r$, with $E|_U\\simeq H^i(E)|_U[-i]$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "If $f:Y\\to X$ factors through $U$, these finite free descriptions\npull back to show that $Lf^*E$ has the required form. Conversely,\nif $Lf^*E$ has that form, for any $y\\in Y$ with image $x$ its\nderived fibre equals\n$(E\\otimes^{\\mathbf L}\\kappa(x))\\otimes_{\\kappa(x)}\\kappa(y)$.\nExtension of fields is faithfully flat and preserves dimensions,\nso $x$ satisfies exactly the defining condition of $U$. Thus the\nimage of $f$ is contained in $U$, which is equivalent to factoring\nthrough that open subscheme.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
